WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.216
In about a minute, you will plan a night of lights, and get a driving route.

00:00:04.216 --> 00:00:05.207
We start on the map.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.396
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.373 --> 00:00:13.805
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:16.304
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.304 --> 00:00:17.654
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.464 --> 00:00:21.832
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.832 --> 00:00:22.529
Tap Allow.

00:00:26.998 --> 00:00:28.529
Choose what you want to see.

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:29.691
Tap the season button.

00:00:32.485 --> 00:00:34.482
Tap Thanksgiving and Christmas Lights.

00:00:36.643 --> 00:00:39.237
On a place you want to visit, tap the heart.

00:00:39.237 --> 00:00:39.813
Add three.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.747
Tap My night.

00:00:46.747 --> 00:00:51.353
Your stops are here, in a sensible driving order, with the miles and the time.

00:00:53.466 --> 00:00:55.877
Choose your maps app, and tap Open route.

00:00:55.877 --> 00:00:57.599
Your maps app takes you there.

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:01.664
Tap Share to send your night to a friend.

00:01:03.303 --> 00:01:05.242
Tap the heart on places you like.

00:01:05.242 --> 00:01:06.783
My night builds the route.

00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:09.236
Then open it in your maps app, or share it.

00:01:10.635 --> 00:01:12.864
Next up: Weekly lights email.
